% Curated overrides for the Notrump Openings lesson.
%
% This preamble is not shipped: package_results.py keeps the generated file's
% preamble and merges only the boards below (board-by-board, curated wins).
%
% Board 3 — issue #35. The source HTML deals South 15 HCP
% (S QJT / H AQ / D T87 / C AQT95) while the narrative teaches the 16-point
% invitation decision and says "with 15 points you decline invitations". A
% student counting correctly passes, which is the opposite of the lesson.
%
% Fix: swap South's CT for East's CJ, giving South C AQJ95 = 16 HCP. The jack
% is a working card opposite North's CK83, and the spot cards the narrative
% praises (ST, DT, C9) all survive. The defect is in the original Baker Bridge
% HTML, not in our pipeline, so this is an override rather than a parser fix.

